jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.8.20~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * Fixed: creating a VM could fail with ten identical "disk id collision"
    lines and then blame allocations from other nodes, on a single-node
    install. A volume deleted from PowerStore Manager stays in the recycle
    bin: no listing shows it and the array still refuses its name. alloc_image
    asked the array which ids were free on every round, got the same answer,
    and rebuilt the identical name until it gave up. The retry now remembers
    which ids were refused and skips them, so it converges whatever is holding
    the name. Reported by Alexander Gott (@alexandergott-afk) in issue #9.
  * Fixed: the message for that failure named a cause it had not established
    and advised retrying something that could never succeed. Losing a race to
    another node and a name the array refuses while its listing shows it free
    are now told apart, and the second names the recycle bin as a thing to
    check rather than asserting it.
  * The same 'exclude' argument was added to PowerFlex's own _find_free_diskid,
    which inherits nothing from BlockBase, so the two signatures stay
    identical.
  * docs/RELEASE_TESTING.md gained the hardware cases these reports produced,
    including the per-VM volume group checks, in both languages.

