jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.8.14~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * Fixed: a forked process still leaked its management session. 0.8.10
    stopped caching the client when PVE::RESTEnvironment->is_worker is true,
    but that flag is set only in fork_worker.s child - PVE.s label for one
    kind of fork. Any other forked child cached a client and ended with
    POSIX::_exit, which runs no DESTROY and no END. Only the process that
    loaded the plugin caches a client now; anything reached through fork
    builds one per call and returns its session when the call returns.
    Measured by a customer on an ME4024 at one session per pvestatd poll.
  * Added: a dedicated ME account with a short per-user session timeout in
    docs/CONFIGURATION (about 180 concurrent sessions down to about 16, as
    measured by the customer), including the ME CLI quoting trap; and a
    session-accumulation entry in docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.

