jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.8.12~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * Fixed: a snapshot rollback flushed and invalidated whatever the device
    lookup handed it, without the kernel confirmation the config-backup and
    transfer paths already require. Devices are resolved fresh from a WWID on
    every use and the lookup has fallbacks; a rollback writes, so a wrong
    device means the flush lands on another volume and this one keeps dirty
    pages that are then written over the restored snapshot. Rollback now
    refuses an unconfirmed device before flushing anything.
  * deactivate_storage reports and skips an unconfirmable device instead of
    dying, because it is a loop over every volume.

