jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.8.9~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * Fixed: management sessions were opened and never given back, reported
    from a customer's PowerVault ME where they accumulate. An ME session
    occupies one of a small number of slots, lives out its idle timeout, and
    the ME CLI has no command to clear one. _logout existed for all four
    families and nothing called it. It is now called when a process exits (an
    END block, because DESTROY runs too late) and when the TTL replaces a
    session - the case every _logout got wrong, because it began with "return
    unless the session is valid" and a session past our own TTL is not.
    Both paths are guarded on the process id so a forked worker cannot end
    its parent's session. GET /exit is NOT VERIFIED against hardware; `show
    sessions` on the array is how to see it work.

