jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.8.1~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * Fixed: a migrated VM could arrive on a node that could not see its disk.
    activate_volume took the host name as final, and on a node that had not
    yet resolved which host object it is - because the array's hosts were
    adopted rather than created - that is the generated name, which does not
    exist on the array. The host object is now resolved before the volume is
    mapped to it, on the path where the volume is not mapped yet.
  * Fixed: a new volume was mapped only to the node that created it. The
    other nodes are found by the pve-<cluster>- prefix, which cannot find an
    adopted host. Each node now publishes the host object it resolved to in
    the cluster filesystem, one file per node, and the pre-mapping reads
    them.

