jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.97~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * Fixed: "the initiator is already registered" now names the host that
    holds it. PowerStore allows an initiator on exactly one host object and
    its refusal names neither the initiator nor the holder, so the plugin
    asks the array who owns each of this node's ports and says so, with the
    two ways out - rename that host to the name the plugin uses, keeping its
    initiators and mappings, or remove it. The message also explains that
    volumes reach the other nodes' hosts through the pve-<cluster>- prefix,
    so a host outside that convention breaks mapping and live migration.
  * Fixed: initiators are compared by identity rather than spelling. The same
    port is written 21:00:f4:c7:aa:a0:a2:50 by PowerStore, 0x2100f4c7aaa0a250
    by sysfs and 2100f4c7aaa0a250 by an ME, and a string comparison would
    re-add an initiator the host already had, which the array refuses.

