    stopped `pvesm add` outright with "the format of the port name ... is
    incorrect. Please use a valid IQN for iSCSI, WWN for FC, or NQN for
    NVMe" - the array quoting the HOST name back where the port name belongs.
    PowerStore requires 21:00:00:0e:1e:1d:2b:3c, the form Dell's own
    ansible-powerstore module documents. Common::FC has always had both
    spellings and every caller had picked the run-together one. The three
    families need three different formats and now send three: PowerStore
    colon-separated, PowerVault run-together (the only form an array has
    accepted), Unity the node WWN and port WWN joined.
  * Fixed: Unity's FC initiator was missing the node WWN entirely. The pair
    is read from one sysfs directory, because two ports of one adapter share
    a node name and pairing two deduplicated lists by position would attach
    the wrong one. NOT VERIFIED against a Unity.
  * Fixed: "Odd number of elements in hash assignment" on a failed pvesm add,
    introduced in 0.7.94 - stale_temp_clones takes named options and was
    called with a bare 0, so the 15-minute grace stayed in force.

