jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.95~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * Fixed: volume_has_feature('sparseinit') promised something a thick volume
    does not do. PVE acts on that feature by NOT writing zeroes - a clone of
    a running VM is mirrored with zero-initialized, pbs-restore gets
    --skip-zero - which is correct for a thin volume and wrong for a thick
    one, whose extents are whatever the array last had there. Answered per
    family now: PowerStore always, Unity and PowerFlex from unity-thin and
    pflex-thick, PowerVault not at all (an ME volume's provisioning depends
