jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.93~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * Fixed: pve-dell-config-get could not find the array password. It parses
    storage.cfg itself, and 0.7.86 moved the password to
    /etc/pve/priv/storage/<storeid>.pw without telling it - so for four
    releases it reported "no credentials configured" for every storage
    following the current convention, at the moment someone was recovering a
    VM configuration. It reads the priv file now, same precedence as the
    plugin, and names the directory it looked in when it finds nothing.
  * Fixed: pve-dell-config-get ignored dell-host-mode. With 'shared' the
    plugin registers one host object for the whole cluster; the tool always
    built the per-node name, so it looked for a host that does not exist and
    then registered a new one carrying this node's initiators. An initiator
    belongs to one host object on these arrays, so at worst that moves it off
    the shared host every node's volumes are mapped to. It reads the mode,
    accepts --host-mode in recover mode, and prints the host object it will
    use before acting on it.
  * Added t/22-config-get.t, which drives the real script as a subprocess
    against a temporary /etc/pve. Nothing tested this tool before.

