jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.89~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * Fixed: starting a VM stat'ed its disk without a time limit.
    qemu_blockdev_options was inherited from PVE's base class, which reaches
    the device through File::stat::stat($path) - an unbounded stat on a path
    under /dev. On a dm-multipath device whose paths have all failed while
    queueing is still on, that is uninterruptible sleep no signal clears, in
    the pvedaemon worker starting the VM. Overridden in all four families,
    answering host_device with the path and no stat, as LVMPlugin and
    RBDPlugin do. The override also refuses to start on the placeholder path
    path() returns when the array cannot be asked.
  * Added: t/15-pve-contract.t asks what LVMPlugin and RBDPlugin - the two
    other block plugins with no filesystem path - both found necessary. A
    base method both of them override is one whose default does not fit that
    shape; inheriting it here now needs a written reason. Against the tree
    two releases ago it names volume_export, volume_import and
    qemu_blockdev_options.

