jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.86~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * SECURITY: the array password was stored in clear text in
    /etc/pve/storage.cfg. This plugin declared a sensitive_properties
    METHOD, but PVE never calls one - it calls
    PVE::Storage::Plugin::sensitive_properties($type) as a FUNCTION and
    looks the answer up in plugindata. So dell-password was never on the
    sensitive list, and the password went into the config file: readable by
    the www-data group, replicated to every node by pmxcfs, returned
    verbatim by GET /storage/<id>, and carried into any /etc/pve backup.
    All four families now declare it in plugindata, and the password is
    written to /etc/pve/priv/storage/<storeid>.pw at mode 0600 - the
    directory PBS uses, 0700 root:www-data, which the web server cannot
    enter.
  * UPGRADING IS SAFE. A storage created before this keeps working: the
    password is read from the priv file if present and from the config
    otherwise, with an hourly reminder. Run
    "pvesm set <storeid> --dell-password '<the password>'" once per storage
    to finish the move - it writes the priv file AND removes the clear-text
    line from storage.cfg in the same operation. An unrelated pvesm set
    never touches the password.

