jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.84~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * UNITY: the multipath settings would have replaced the kernel's
    CLARiiON-family tuning with a generic guess. A conf.d device section
    replaces the built-in entry wholesale, and Unity's drop-in carried the
    generic ALUA block copied from PowerVault. The built-in for ^DGC is
    deliberately different: path_checker emc_clariion with detect_checker
    no pinned (the family checker recognises a passive SP; TUR does not),
    prio emc rather than alua (a Unity can run ALUA or PNR and emc judges
    both - alua on PNR scores both SPs equally and the LUN trespasses back
    and forth between controllers), and NO hardware_handler (forcing
    "1 alua" onto a PNR array breaks its failover). The drop-in now follows
    the built-in and adds only bounded-recovery settings; the product
    pattern widens to ^(RAID|DISK|VRAID); config version 2 upgrades old
    drop-ins automatically. TESTING.md gains the on-hardware check: two
    prio groups in multipath -ll, and no trespass ping-pong in Unisphere.

