jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.75~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * dell-portal takes several comma-separated addresses and the client fails
    over between them. Asked by the ME4024's tester: their array has one
    management IP per controller and no floating address, so a controller
    failover takes the configured address away with it. The data path never
    needed help - dm-multipath and ALUA handle it and running guests never
    notice - but management (status, allocation, snapshots, deletion) failed
    until someone edited the storage by hand. A connection failure the array
    never saw moves to the next address immediately without backoff; the
    answering address becomes sticky; the session is dropped on every
    rotation because a session belongs to the controller that issued it.
    Every address gets at least one try even on the health client, so pvesm
    status's worst case is one short timeout per address. One address
    behaves exactly as before. All four families inherit the feature.
  * Found while testing it: the request URL was built once, outside the
    retry loop, so a rotated portal would still have sent every retry to the
    dead address. It is now built per attempt.
  * The bound is enforced: nested request layers each cycling the address
    list turned a 2-second status timeout into 21 seconds on a dead array.
    Once one request has watched every address fail to connect, a flag stops
    the layers above from cycling the same dead set. Measured: two dead
    addresses at dell-status-timeout 2 cost pvesm status 4.0 seconds - one
    timeout per address, exactly the documented worst case.

