jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.74~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * UNITY: the rollback backup snapshot from 0.7.71 carried two traps of its
    own. Being the newest snapshot on the volume and visible to PVE, it made
    volume_rollback_is_possible refuse every SECOND rollback with "not the
    most recent snapshot" - blocking the operation it exists to protect. And
    its snapshot name was 'rollback', a name a PVE user can type; a user
    snapshot by that name would have been deleted by the cleanup. The
    backups are now filtered from what PVE sees (the purge does not come
    through that path, so nothing is orphaned), named 'pve.rollback' with a
    dot PVE forbids in snapshot names so no user can ever collide, and
    capped at one - the previous backup is removed before each restore
    instead of accumulating invisibly forever. The test creates a user
    snapshot actually called 'rollback', rolls back twice, and asserts it
    survives; reverting the fix fails four tests.

