jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.52~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * A snapshot named 'before-s-after' - which PVE accepts - decoded as a
    snapshot of a volume that does not exist on PowerVault and PowerFlex,
    whose snapshot separator is '-s-'. It was invisible to
    volume_snapshot_list and missed by the purge that has to run before a
    volume can be deleted, so deleting that volume would have failed with
    "it still has snapshots" and no way to see which. The separator was
    matched greedily, taking the last '-s-'; matching lazily would take the
    first and break a storage whose id sanitises to 's', whose volume names
    contain '-s-' themselves. The volume half is matched by its actual shape
    now.
  * A snapshot name the array would ALTER rather than shorten is refused
    instead of being silently renamed. PVE keeps the name the user typed, so
    a snapshot stored as 'trailing' when 'trailing-' was asked for is listed
    under a name that does not match the VM configuration, and a later
    'trailing' collides with it. A name that merely does not fit is still
    shortened deterministically - PVE allows 40 characters and a whole
    PowerVault volume name is 32.

 -- Jason Cheng <jason@jason.tools>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 19:04:06 +0800

jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.51~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * Two storage ids that differ only in punctuation produced the same volume
    names. The storeid is folded into the prefix with '-' becoming '_',
    because '-' is the separator inside a volume name; that folding is lossy,
    and 'ps-1', 'ps.1', 'ps+1', 'ps@1' and 'ps__1' all become 'ps_1'. Two such
    storages on one array shared every volume name: each listed the other's
    disks, the ownership gate passed for both, and deleting a disk from one
    deleted it from the other. It cannot be fixed inside the name - a whole
    PowerVault volume name is 32 characters - so on_add_hook refuses to create
    a storage whose prefix matches an existing one, naming the other storage
    and what to change. Verified through a real 'pvesm add' on this node.

