jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.50~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * A protocol a storage type cannot speak is refused when it is configured.
    'dell-protocol' is declared once for all three types, because
    PVE::SectionConfig dies on a duplicate property name and takes every
    storage on the node with it - so its enum lists every protocol any family
    supports. PowerStore accepted 'sdc' and PowerFlex accepted 'fc'.
    PowerFlex then died on first use with the storage already added; the SAN
    families were worse and treated the unknown protocol as iSCSI, silently
    and permanently. on_add_hook and on_update_hook now check it, verified
    through a real 'pvesm add' on this node.
  * PowerVault: the transport refuses a command with an empty argument. The
    ME CLI is positional, so an empty argument is not an empty argument - it
    is a command with one fewer and everything after it shifted up. 'unmap
    volume initiator <host> <volume>' with an empty host becomes 'unmap
    volume initiator <volume>', which Dell documents as removing the DEFAULT
    mapping from every host on the array.

