jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.49~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * LXC container snapshots were taken of a live filesystem. PVE::LXC::Config
    freezes a container's mountpoints before a snapshot only when the storage
    answers volume_snapshot_needs_fsfreeze; the base class answers 0 and this
    plugin never overrode it. A container's root is mounted on this host and
    is being written to while the array snapshots it, so the result was
    crash-consistent at best. All three types answer 1 now, as ZFSPlugin -
    the other plugin where an external appliance takes the snapshot - does.
  * Moving a disk to a storage of another type, pvesm export/import and
    remote migration were all refused before reaching any code here.
    storage_migrate asks both storages for their common transfer formats, and
    the base class answers "none" for a storage without a path. LVM and RBD
    are raw block storage without a path too, and both declare raw+size; so
    does this now. Snapshots, and a linked clone on its own, are still
    refused.

