jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.10~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * PowerFlex ran 'nvme connect' for every target the array published on
    every pvestatd poll. Connecting to an address that is already connected
    succeeds, so it worked — but it is one process per address six times a
    minute per node, each carrying a 30 second timeout on a degraded network.
    It now reads the existing paths once and connects only what is missing;
    when everything is connected it forks nothing at all. A target that stays
    unreachable is retried on the rescan interval rather than every poll,
    unless no path is up at all, in which case it is retried immediately.
  * The storage pool check in activate_storage is rate-limited for the same
    reason. status() looks the pool up again on the same poll to report
    capacity, so doing it in both places was one duplicated listing of every
    pool on the array, six times a minute per node.

